# Local validation evidence is private operator material. Canonical fixtures and
# the validation protocol remain tracked; individual run records do not.
validation/runs/*
!validation/runs/_README.md

# Benchmark run records, for the same reason: a measured result belongs to one machine
# on one day. The case definitions in benchmarks/arbench/ are the tracked artefact.
benchmarks/results/

# The mutation harness records the bytes a mutation replaced, so an interrupted run can
# restore the tree. The marker is machine-local recovery state, never an artefact: if one
# is present the tree is mid-mutation and the next run will restore it. AR-222 upgraded
# this from a digest-only marker to a stash of the actual bytes, because `finally` does not
# run when a process is killed from outside and a digest alone cannot undo anything.
.ariadne-mutation-restore.json
.ariadne-mutation-restore/
